A||N||22||bHooper||as promised... pics of the new SE!||||10||
Z||000000||bHooper||05-24-2001||10:30 PM||||you couldnt tell by looking at it, but this car has 158,000 miles on it!<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Mvc-001f_4.jpg"> <BR>it runs great, but does have an exhaust leak in the rear manifold, and the tranny mounts need replacing.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Mvc-005f_7.jpg"> <P>the seats are original GM!  they have leather side bolsters and vinyl inserts.  i haven't seen anything else like them.  the dirvers seat is realy worn, the future Mrs. bHooper has promised me MrMikes seats for xmas!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Mvc-006f_11.jpg"> <P>i got the car from Doug Kinney, on Monday.  i flew into Pittsburgh (Doug was kind enough to pick me up) at 8:30 am, and after a little work on the cruise control, left the "Fiero Warehouse" around 12:30.  7 hours (and 400 miles) later, i was back in Greensboro.<P>i spent 2 days working on the brakes, changing the oil, and tranny fluid/filter.  i still need to remove the tint (it's way to dark for NC) and fix the exhaust leak b4 i can get it inspected.<P>the car drives great!  Doug lowered it with the Belltech spindles (2" drop in the front!), probably a little to low... it tends to bottom out under heavy braking!<P>Anyway, hope everyone likes my new future daily driver!<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Mvc-007f_6.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Mvc-002f_13.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT 5 speed<BR>*Black '86 SE Automatic||||reg||10
