Z||000002||bHooper||05-24-2001||10:34 PM||||sorry about the size of the pics... how do you adjust them?  my friend took the pics with his new digital camera.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||84Bill||05-24-2001||11:11 PM||||     <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by bHooper:<BR><B>sorry about the size of the pics... how do you adjust them?  my friend took the pics with his new digital camera.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I use MS word to resize mine, I "Insert" the pictures I want then save it as a web page. Word will create a folder called XXXX_Files where the X's are the name of the document. In the XXXX_Files there will be 2 times the number of pictures, image001.jpg , image002.jpg one is the original high res the other is a smaller low res.<BR> <A HREF="http://cn308598-a.wall1.pa.home.com/example11.gif" TARGET=_blank>http://cn308598-a.wall1.pa.home.com/example11.gif</A>     <BR>  <A HREF="http://cn308598-a.wall1.pa.home.com/example12.gif" TARGET=_blank>http://cn308598-a.wall1.pa.home.com/example12.gif</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://cn308598-a.wall1.pa.home.com/example13.gif" TARGET=_blank>http://cn308598-a.wall1.pa.home.com/example13.gif</A> <P>you can see image001.jpg and 002.jpg are the same picture but look at the size difference<P>Cool <BR>I'll just leave links so as not clog the bandwidth but they will be there for your reference, theese are a bit clearer than the posted ones. Gald I could help  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><p>[This message has been edited by 84Bill (edited 05-25-2001).]||||reg||14
